Bob LeChevalier wrote:
> Yanis Batura wrote:
>> There are only 1342 semantic hint classes.
> 
> 
> Most natural languages using a semantic classifier system have a couple 
> orders of magnitude fewer classes (they are commonly called "genders", 
> Swahili has 14, and Russian has only 3), and they work anyway.

The semantic classifier system has nothing to do with gender, which 
Lojban doesn't have. The equivalent of a type-3 fu'ivla is a word like 
"killifish", where the first part has no meaning by itself, and the 
second tells what kind of thing the referent is.

